### HAS_A_Relationship
-- The Has A relationship refers to the situation where on class conatined object of another class.

*** Types of Has- A- Relationship
-- there are two main types of has- A Relationship
1. Aggregation :- The "Friends with Benefits" of object relationship
2. Composition :- The "Till Do us Part" of object connections

**Aggregation :- is a type of HAS_A_Relationship where the contained objects can exist independently in container objects. the represent a weak relationship b/w them.
e.g :- A university HAS-A professor
professor can exist independently of the university.

** Composition:- A composition is Strong type HAS-A-Relationship where the contained the object cannot exist independently of the container object.
--> the represent a strong relationship b/w the object, indiaceting a whole-part Realtionship
--> if conatiner object is destroy then containe object is also destroy.
E>g: HOUSE have a room. so room cannot exist independently of the house.

Note:- i.) whenever you see the solid diamond arrow this is composition object.
       ii.) whenever you see the diamond only arrow this is The aggregate Object.
